      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`FlattenedTensorBucket` packs each input with `tensor.flatten().view(torch.uint8)`. Flattening does not necessarily make a tensor contiguous: `torch.arange(8, dtype=torch.float32)[::2]` retains stride 2, and packing fails with `self.stride(-1) must be 1 to view Float as Byte`.\n\n## Modifications\n\nMake each flattened tensor contiguous before its byte view. This supports strided weight views without changing bucket metadata or the wire layout. Already-contiguous inputs need no additional copy from `contiguous()`.\n\nAdd exact CPU round-trip coverage for FP32, BF16 and FP16 tensors across contiguous, strided-vector, strided-matrix, transposed, scalar and empty layouts. Check names, dtype, shape, values and packed bytes.\n\nRelated #39264 optimizes receive-buffer allocation; this change is limited to sender packing and does not alter its allocation API or the mixed-dtype alignment contract.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Before: six strided cases error on the original implementation.\n- After: all 18 dtype/layout combinations pass with exact values and bytes.\n- Repository pre-commit checks pass for both changed files, including registered-test validation.\n\nDirect validation of this exact PR head now passes on macOS with Python 3.12.14 and PyTorch 2.13.0: the committed registered test runs unchanged through normal package imports, without the earlier namespace bootstrap. All 18 dtype/layout combinations pass. With only the bucket module reverted to the parent implementation, the same test reports six expected strided-input errors; restoring the PR module restores a passing run. No source changes were needed for this validation.\n\nUpstream CI remains unrun: 13 workflow runs (including Base and Lint) report `action_required`; the two successful checks only update labels and PR metadata. No CUDA transfer, full-model weight update, or inference-accuracy run was performed. The reproduction is a CPU tensor-utility failure, not a measured production-model failure.\n\nInstalled development environment test command:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=python python test/registered/rl/test_tensor_bucket_strides.py\n```\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot run. Strided inputs require a contiguous copy before byte packing; no end-to-end performance improvement is claimed.\n\nAI assistance: Codex investigated the issue, implemented the fix and tests, and ran local validation.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37076307089](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37076307089)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37076306971](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37076306971)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37076307227](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37076307227)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
